.Dd February 6, 2026
.Dt VOP_MKDIR 9
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm vop_mkdir
.Nd create a directory
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/param.h
.In sys/vnode.h
.Ft int
.Fn vop_mkdir "struct vnode *dvp" "struct vnode **vpp" "const char *name" "mode_t mode" "struct ucred *cred"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn vop_mkdir
function creates a new directory named
.Fa name
in the directory
.Fa dvp .
If successful, the new directory vnode is returned in
.Fa *vpp
with a reference count incremented.
.Pp
Arguments:
.Bl -tag -width ".Fa cred"
.It Fa dvp
The parent directory vnode.
.It Fa vpp
Pointer to a vnode pointer where the new directory vnode will be stored.
.It Fa name
The name of the new directory.
.It Fa mode
The mode (permissions) for the new directory.
.It Fa cred
The user credentials for the operation.
.El
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Returns 0 on success, or an error code on failure.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width ".Bq Er EOPNOTSUPP"
.It Bq Er EOPNOTSUPP
The filesystem does not support this operation.
.It Bq Er ENOTDIR
The vnode
.Fa dvp
is not a directory.
.It Bq Er EEXIST
The directory already exists.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr vnode 9 ,
.Xr vop_create 9
